Divergence
----------

IRIN is a hard fork, not a downstream distribution. It does not track upstream
releases and does not open pull requests against upstream. Its direction,
release train, and package identity are its own.

Work that originates in IRIN rather than upstream is, at the time of writing,
concentrated in the measurement layer: declared engineering assertions, the
geometry evaluator that scores artifacts against them, the benchmark corpus and
runner, and the repair accounting built on top. Where IRIN adds new files, they
carry IRIN's own copyright. Where IRIN modifies inherited files, the upstream
copyright stands alongside.
